    <!-- User Guide Dialog -->
    <string name="guide_title">Music Drop User Guide</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_title">1. Downloading from links &amp; playlists</string>
    <string name="guide_s1_body">• Paste any link in «Download» or use «Share → Music Drop» from YouTube, Spotify, Apple Music, Deezer, Amazon Music, or SoundCloud.\n• On playlists and albums, the app checks your library first and automatically selects only missing songs («Missing only» button).\n• If a YouTube URL includes a timestamp (?t=…), it is applied as the trim start.\n• In the queue you can «Pause / Resume queue», view overall progress, edit Title/Artist/Album, trim Start/End, switch editions in «Versions», or edit/search lyrics in «Lyrics».</string>
    <string name="guide_s2_title">2. Search &amp; microphone recognition</string>
    <string name="guide_s2_body">• In «Search» you can search YouTube, preview by tapping ▶ on the thumbnail, and trim from the current playback second with one tap.\n• Tap the microphone button (🎙️) to listen to ~5.5 seconds of ambient music and automatically identify the song (100% free, no account needed) to download it or browse versions.</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_title">3. History &amp; mini-player</string>
    <string name="guide_s3_body">• In «History» you can search and play your saved songs (both local and from your NAS).\n• Tap any song to view «Details»: cover art, embedded lyrics, LUFS normalization check, file size, and full path (tap the path to copy).\n• The bottom mini-player lets you skip (⏮ / ⏭) through history with auto-advance and tap the title to jump back to the list.</string>
    <string name="guide_s4_title">4. Audio quality &amp; organization</string>
    <string name="guide_s4_body">• Everything is normalized without clipping (true-peak limiter) to your chosen LUFS target:\n  - -16 (Soft): more natural dynamics (classical, acoustic, Hi‑Fi).\n  - -14 (Standard): Spotify/YouTube standard; ideal balance.\n  - -11 (Loud): more volume and punch (car or Bluetooth speakers).\n• MP3 192k or 320k encoding with ID3v2.3 tags, 600×600 cover art, and embedded lyrics.\n• If you trim the end of a song, a smooth 250 ms fade-out is applied automatically.\n• In «Settings» you can choose your NAS (auto Local/Remote switching) or your phone\'s Music/ folder, flat, by Artist, or Artist/Album.</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_title">5. NAS connection (Local, VPN or SMB port)</string>
    <string name="guide_s5_body">• Local IP (port 445): use it for fast uploads on your home Wi‑Fi.\n• Remote IP / Tailscale + Port (445 default): works for Tailscale, another VPN (WireGuard/ZeroTier), or an external IP/DDNS domain with a forwarded port on your router (host:port format is also supported).\n• For security, when connecting from outside your home network, a VPN (Tailscale/WireGuard) is recommended instead of exposing SMB directly to the internet.</string>

